{"id":"NCT06989437","title":"A Study to Learn About the Medicine Ponsegromab in Adults With Cancer of the Pancreas Which Has Spread and Caused Significant Body Weight Loss and Fatigue","official":"A Phase 2b/3, Randomized, Double-Blind Study to Investigate the Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of Ponsegromab (PF-06946860) Compared With Placebo Both With Background First-Line Chemotherapy in Adult Participants With Cachexia and Metastatic Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma","summary":"Study to investigate the efficacy, safety and tolerability of systemic chemotherapy plus ponsegromab versus systemic chemotherapy plus placebo for the first-line treatment in adult participants with cachexia and metastatic pancreatic ductal adenocardinoma.","conditions":["Cachexia","Metastatic Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"ponsegromab"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"placebo"}],"criteria":"Key inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Signed Informed Consent Document\n* Documented active diagnosis of metastatic pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma\n* Cachexia defined by Fearon criteria of weight loss\n* Completed 1 x 28-day cycle of first-line systemic nab-paclitaxel and gemcitabine chemotherapy or 2 x 14-day cycles of FOLFIRINOX chemotherapy and prior to receiving Cycle 2 chemotherapy\n* ECOG PS ≤1 with life expectancy of at least 4 months\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria:\n\n* Current active reversible causes of decreased food intake\n* Cachexia caused by other reasons\n* Any prior or current clinical diagnosis of heart failure, irrespective of left ventricular ejection fraction or New York Heart Association classification\n* Left ventricular ejection fraction \\<50%\n* Receiving tube feedings or parenteral nutrition at the time of Screening or Randomization\n* History of allergic or anaphylactic reaction to any therapeutic or diagnostic monoclonal antibody\n* History of allergy or hypersensitivity to any of the chemotherapeutics or any of their excipients\n* Neuroendocrine (carcinoid, islet cell) or acinar pancreatic carcinoma, symptomatic brain metastasis, leptomeningeal disease or other active CNS metastases\n* Inadequate liver function\n* Renal disease requiring dialysis or eGFR \\<30 mL/min/1.73m2","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":982,"start":"2025-10-03","pcd":"2028-01-23","upd":"2026-10-14","sponsor":"Pfizer","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Pfizer CT.gov Call Center · 1-800-718-1021 · ClinicalTrials.gov_Inquiries@pfizer.com"],"sites":[{"f":"The Kirklin Clinic of UAB Hospital","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35233","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":""},{"f":"The University of Alabama at Birmingham","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35294","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":""},{"f":"Mayo Clinic Hospital","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85054","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":""},{"f":"Central Arkansas Radiation Therapy Institute, dba CARTI","city":"Bryant","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72022","s":"R","lat":34.5959,"lon":-92.4891,"c":""},{"f":"Central Arkansas Radiation Therapy Institute, dba CARTI","city":"Conway","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72034","s":"R","lat":35.0887,"lon":-92.4421,"c":""},{"f":"CARTI Cancer Center","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72205","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":""},{"f":"Central Arkansas Radiation Therapy Institute, dba CARTI","city":"North Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72117","s":"R","lat":34.7695,"lon":-92.2671,"c":""},{"f":"Central Arkansas Radiation Therapy Institute, dba CARTI","city":"Pine Bluff","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"71603","s":"R","lat":34.2284,"lon":-92.0032,"c":""},{"f":"UC San Diego Medical Center - Encinitas","city":"Encinitas","pr":"California","zip":"92024","s":"R","lat":33.037,"lon":-117.292,"c":""},{"f":"Chao Family Comprehensive Cancer Center and Ambulatory Care","city":"Irvine","pr":"California","zip":"92612","s":"R","lat":33.6695,"lon